  "source_excerpts": [
    {
      "end": 6,
      "hash": "21a952302624f808b1450bb9910245607741471ed3e8401a4cd53b74932d267a",
      "source": "corpus/qualification/activities/run.yaml",
      "start": 1,
      "text": "id: run\nsteps:\n  - id: delivery\n    routine:\n      name: deliver\n      arguments: {envelope: sealed}"
    },
    {
      "end": 14,
      "hash": "0c5b2c9f9813d5f4545fc938f1a0e41b167b3ad6e450db95f35a0f3ef6084025",
      "source": "corpus/canon/resources/anti-patterns.md",
      "start": 1,
      "text": "# Controlled qualification anti-patterns\n\nThese two entries are test criteria, not the project's full canon. Interpret only the binding and instruction constructs defined here. Each distinct failing instruction or binding is one finding; section and whole-element rows can expose the same finding.\n\n## Controlled Qualification\n\n### AP-01. emission-without-validation\n\nDetect: A technique's Protocol instruction or Rules clause explicitly directs an artifact's emission without validating that artifact first. Review each instruction and each semicolon-separated clause independently. Validation elsewhere does not excuse an instruction or clause that explicitly permits unvalidated emission.\n\nDo not flag: A directive to validate before emission satisfies this criterion. A heading, output declaration, retention clause, destination declaration, routine call, binding or graph label does not itself direct emission. Capability descriptions describe the service and are not imperative instructions.\n\nFix: Require validation of the same artifact before emission in every emitting instruction and clause.\n"
    },
    {
      "end": 12,
      "hash": "53367edcf890fd3d39b34e55f325affa64db1663fe33b1aeefb8796519bf8f77",
